  "answer": "Found it and fixed. The bug was in the URL, not the method.\n\n**Why it failed:** `deleteFromCart` built `DELETE /api/v1/cart/{cartID}/product/{item.id}` \u2014 using the product's numeric **ID**. The Shopizer backend endpoint (`@DeleteMapping(\"/cart/{code}/product/{sku}\")` in `ShoppingCartApi`, matched by `product.getSku().equals(sku)` in `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.removeShoppingCartItem`) interprets that path segment as the product **SKU** (a string). When a catalog's SKUs differ from product IDs, no line item matches, the backend silently re-saves the unchanged cart and returns 204 \u2014 so removing an item \"does nothing.\" Notably, `addToCart` in the same file already identifies products by `item.sku`, and the cart JSON includes an `sku` field on each line item.\n\n**Fix:** in [cartActions.js](~/code/benchmark/okf-local/main/no_okf/work/g1_delete_item/no_okf/codex/3/src/redux/actions/cartActions.js:163), changed the delete URL to use `item.sku` instead of `item.id`. That's the only file modified.\n\n**Files used:**\n- `src/redux/actions/cartActions.js` \u2014 read and edited\n- `src/util/constant.js`, `src/util/webService.js` \u2014 to confirm the request path and transport\n- `src/pages/other/Cart.js`, `src/redux/reducers/cartReducer.js` \u2014 to confirm the cart item shape and UI behavior\n- `public/env-config.js` \u2014 to identify the API version (`/api/v1/`)\n- Backend source (Shopizer, fetched read-only for diagnosis): `ShoppingCartApi.java`, `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`, `ReadableShoppingCartItem`/`ProductEntity` models and the cart mapper",
